name":"9…Nfxd4","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"9…Nfxd4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the bishop on d4.","The next best move, 9…b6, would drop Black's winning chances from 56% to 44% (+0.64).","9…Nfxd4 trades knight for bishop.","Trades knight for bishop.","The knight on d4 can be taken by the c3 pawn or the knight on f3.","White answers 10.cxd4, taking back and taking e5 away from the knight on c6."]},{"ply":38,"name":"19…Rd8","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"19…Rd8! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Protects the d5 pawn, which was hanging.","The next best move, 19…Ne7, would drop Black's winning chances from 76% to 54% (−0.47).","19…Rd8 stops Qxd5+.","White was threatening Qxd5+, winning a pawn. Rd8 takes care of it.","White answers 20.Bb1.","Engine line: 20.Bb1 Kh8 21.Qa3 Rf7 22.Kh1 e4 (−3.10)."]},{"ply":42,"name":"21…Bxf2+","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","headline":"21…Bxf2+!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the bishop on f2 where it can be taken.","White can take, but after 22.Kxf2 Qxg5 23.Kg1 Rxf3 the engine rates it −5.17.","Takes the pawn on f2.","Creates a passed pawn on e5: no enemy pawn can stop it any more.","21…Bxf2+ wins a knight for a rook.","Takes the f2 pawn and wins a knight for a rook once the captures settle."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"21…Bxf2+!! offers the bishop on f2. Taking it gives Black the material back and more."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"21…Bxf2+ puts the bishop on f2 where it can be taken by the king. That's a bishop on offer."},{"title":"If White takes the bishop","text":"22.Kxf2 is met by 22…Qxg5, taking the knight on g5. Then 23…Nd4 threatens …Nxb3, winning the queen for a rook, and 24…Qg4 adds pressure on the knight on f3. Black ends up a pawn ahead: Black is winning (−4.36). This is White's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 21…Kh8, is clearly weaker (−3.59 against −5.17). White answers 22.Rxc6, taking the knight on c6 and threatening Rxh6, winning the queen for a rook. Black would still be winning, but far less than after 21…Bxf2+."}]},{"ply":44,"name":"22…Qxg5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"22…Qxg5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the knight on g5.","Shores up the e5 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (2 against 1).","The next best move, 22…Nd4, would drop Black's winning chances from 87% to 51% (−0.11).","22…Qxg5 wins a knight for 6 points of material.","Takes the knight on g5 and wins a knight for 6 points of material once the captures settle.","White answers 23.Kg1, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on g7 and a king with pawns missing from its shelter."]},{"ply":46,"name":"23…Rxf3","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"23…Rxf3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the knight on f3.","Protects the queen on g5, which was hanging.","The next best move, 23…Qf6, would drop Black's winning chances from 86% to 74% (−2.87).","23…Rxf3 threatens …e4, winning the exchange.","It threatens …e4, winning the exchange, so White has to spend the next move on it.","White answers 24.Bxh7+, taking the h7 pawn and uncovering an attack on the rook on f3, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on g7 and a king with pawns missing from its shelter."]},{"ply":60,"name":"30…Be2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"30…Be2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked bishop to safety.","Protects the e5 pawn, which was hanging.","The next best move, 30…Bf5, would drop Black's winning chances from 84% to 69% (−2.23).","30…Be2 gets the bishop out of the way of hxg4.","White was threatening hxg4, winning a bishop. The bishop steps away.","White answers 31.Re3, winning a bishop for a rook."]},{"ply":72,"name":"36…Kf6","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"36…Kf6! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The next best move, 36…a5, would drop Black's winning chances from 82% to 62% (−1.33).","36…Kf6 prepares …Rf1+ and …Ke5.","The engine's plan continues with …Rf1+ and …Ke5: this move is the first step.","White answers 37.h4.","Engine line: 37.h4 Rf1+ 38.Ke3 Ke5 39.Rd2 Rh1 (−4.71)."]},{"ply":80,"name":"40…Rb1","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"40…Rb1! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the b2 pawn, which is undefended.","Moves the attacked rook to safety.","The next best move, 40…Rg1, would drop Black's winning chances from 88% to 77% (−3.29).","40…Rb1 gets the rook out of the way of Kxf1.","White was threatening Kxf1, winning a rook. The rook steps away.","The rook takes the half-open b-file."]}],"opening":{"name":"Caro-Kann Defense: Advance Variation, Botvinnik-Carls Defense","eco":"B12","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 9.Bd3: 17 moves in all, 9 by White and 8 by Black.","Theory runs out after 9.Bd3: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}